Answer: A basic Java program contains a class, and the main method is placed inside the class.

```java
public class Greet {
public static void main(String[] args) {
System.out.println("Namaskara Karnataka");
}
}
```

Answer: A class boundary is the area between the opening and closing curly braces of a class. For example:

```java
class Greet {
}
```

Methods are placed within this boundary.

Answer: print() prints the content without moving the cursor to the next line. println() prints the content and moves the cursor to the next line. For example:

```java
System.out.print("Hello");
System.out.print("World");
```

produces: HelloWorld Whereas:

```java
System.out.println("Hello");
System.out.println("World");
```

produces: Hello World
